WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.172 --> 00:00:16.255
Tom had finished telling Joe and Huck about his trip to town, Joe and Huck were ready to

2
00:00:16.295 --> 00:00:16.715
go home.

3
00:00:18.497 --> 00:00:22.720
Even Tom was tired of playing pirates and swimming, but he simply wasn't ready to return.

4
00:00:23.861 --> 00:00:27.464
Sure, he was homesick, and he thought of Aunt Polly and Becky all the time.

5
00:00:28.405 --> 00:00:31.628
But Tom now had a plan to make his return home a grand entrance.

6
00:00:33.052 --> 00:00:36.693
It meant waiting a while longer, and it meant the other boys would have to wait too.

7
00:00:37.573 --> 00:00:39.714
Tom didn't want to tell his friends about his plan yet.

8
00:00:40.594 --> 00:00:44.395
He was afraid that even his amazing plan would not be enough to keep them on the island.

9
00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:49.957
So he had to keep them interested in their adventure a little longer, even though it wouldn't be

10
00:00:50.057 --> 00:00:55.298
easy. Tom saw that Joe was sad, so he tried to cheer him up.

11
00:00:55.318 --> 00:00:59.139
"Let's look for buried treasure again," he said.

12
00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.220
But Huck and Joe didn't want to look for treasure again.

13
00:01:03.468 --> 00:01:05.670
Finally Joe said, "Let's give up.

14
00:01:06.571 --> 00:01:07.772
I want to go home."

15
00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:11.275
"Oh no," said Tom.

16
00:01:11.295 --> 00:01:13.757
"Just think of all the fishing here."

17
00:01:13.777 --> 00:01:17.160
"I don't care about fishing.

18
00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:21.604
I want to go home," said Joe, and he started to cry.

19
00:01:21.624 --> 00:01:24.466
"What a baby," teased Tom.

20
00:01:24.486 --> 00:01:26.808
"You miss your mother, I bet."

21
00:01:27.609 --> 00:01:33.669
"I do," said Joe, "and you'd miss yours too, if you had one!"

22
00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:36.510
Tom became angry.

23
00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:42.631
"We'll let the crybaby go home, won't we, Huck?"

24
00:01:43.151 --> 00:01:45.092
"Y-yes," replied Huck sadly.

25
00:01:45.112 --> 00:01:46.953
Now Joe was angry.

26
00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:52.194
"Tom Sawyer, I'll never speak to you again for as long as I live!"

27
00:01:52.214 --> 00:01:53.874
"Who cares!"

28
00:01:54.355 --> 00:01:54.995
said Tom.

29
00:01:55.755 --> 00:01:56.395
"Go home.

30
00:01:56.895 --> 00:01:58.416
You're not a very good pirate.

31
00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.021
Huck and I aren't crybabies.

32
00:02:01.622 --> 00:02:03.623
We'll stay, won't we, Huck?"

33
00:02:05.284 --> 00:02:08.967
Tom didn't really want Joe to leave, but he was too angry to think of how he could

34
00:02:09.007 --> 00:02:09.847
make Joe stay.

35
00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:13.110
"I want to go too," said Huck quietly.

36
00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:16.052
"It's so lonely with just the three of us.

37
00:02:17.112 --> 00:02:18.854
If Joe goes, it'll be worse.

38
00:02:19.654 --> 00:02:20.575
Let's go too, Tom."

39
00:02:22.356 --> 00:02:24.297
Huck put on his hat and got ready to leave.

40
00:02:25.338 --> 00:02:27.700
He looked at Tom and said, "Think it over.

41
00:02:28.404 --> 00:02:29.604
We'll wait for you by the raft."

42
00:02:30.745 --> 00:02:32.045
Tom knew he was in trouble.

43
00:02:33.265 --> 00:02:37.427
His plan for a grand entrance was falling apart, and he couldn't think of a way to save

44
00:02:37.507 --> 00:02:41.928
it. "Wait forever if you want," said Tom angrily.

45
00:02:41.948 --> 00:02:43.828
"But I'm not going with you.

46
00:02:44.068 --> 00:02:45.129
I'm staying here."

47
00:02:46.329 --> 00:02:48.450
Joe and Huck began walking toward the raft.

48
00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.551
After a minute Tom ran after them, shouting, "Wait!

49
00:02:54.211 --> 00:02:56.872
Wait! I want to tell you something."

50
00:03:00.052 --> 00:03:02.233
Tom quickly told his friends about his idea.

51
00:03:02.873 --> 00:03:05.815
He promised that they could go home soon, just not today.

52
00:03:07.716 --> 00:03:09.156
Huck and Joe's spirits lifted.

53
00:03:09.176 --> 00:03:12.057
"Really, we'll go home on Sunday?"

54
00:03:12.518 --> 00:03:13.078
asked Joe.

55
00:03:13.618 --> 00:03:17.340
Tom smiled and said, "Yes, on Sunday."

56
00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.721
The boys dived into the river and played all day.

57
00:03:21.602 --> 00:03:25.503
That night they cooked and ate the rest of their food, and they retold the tales of their

58
00:03:25.564 --> 00:03:26.344
great adventure.

59
00:03:27.324 --> 00:03:31.807
Finally Tom explained that on Sunday they would float across the river on a log, so that no

60
00:03:31.867 --> 00:03:32.847
one would see them coming.

61
00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:36.929
Then they would sneak into church and hide under the large table by the entrance.

62
00:03:39.371 --> 00:03:43.093
On Sunday the whole town gathered in the church for Tom, Joe, and Huck's funeral.

63
00:03:44.894 --> 00:03:47.435
Everyone knew the boys, and they were all quite sad.

64
00:03:48.656 --> 00:03:49.936
Becky was the saddest of all.

65
00:03:49.956 --> 00:03:53.798
"Being mad was silly," she thought.

66
00:03:53.818 --> 00:03:56.580
"Now I'll never see Tom again."

67
00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.003
Aunt Polly and Joe's mother were sitting in the front of the church, and they were both dressed

68
00:04:02.043 --> 00:04:02.503
in black.

69
00:04:04.304 --> 00:04:07.767
After the opening prayer and hymn, the minister spoke about the boys.

70
00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.609
He told many stories about their good deeds.

71
00:04:11.649 --> 00:04:16.072
When the minister finished speaking, everyone was crying—even the minister himself.

72
00:04:19.254 --> 00:04:23.497
Earlier that morning the boys had hidden themselves under the table by the entrance of the church.

73
00:04:24.878 --> 00:04:26.960
They waited for the minister to finish his speech.

74
00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.341
Then they emerged from under the table.

75
00:04:32.641 --> 00:04:35.642
Tom proudly led his friends down the main aisle of the church.

76
00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:37.883
Everyone was shocked!

77
00:04:38.923 --> 00:04:43.365
Aunt Polly and Joe's mother shouted for joy, and they kissed the three boys wildly.

78
00:04:44.165 --> 00:04:46.746
Everyone else greeted the boys with relief and delight.

79
00:04:47.526 --> 00:04:52.568
The minister asked everyone to sing a hymn of thanksgiving, and the singing nearly took the church's roof

80
00:04:52.768 --> 00:04:52.888
off.
